From f28af974d134ecd223bc3129e003ba06c6c93b3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkirby <rkirby@nvidia.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:44:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Gate the parity QKV path on InferenceMode, not eval mode

SelfAttention.get_query_key_value_tensors used 'not self.training', but
NeMo RL runs eval-mode forwards on the training model: get_logprobs_presharded
calls model.eval(), so the trainer's logprob pass entered the parity QKV path
and handed vLLM-layout tensors to TE's context-parallel flash attention,
failing with SystemError inside AttnFuncWithCPAndKVP2P (smoke 4050516).
InferenceMode.is_active() is the gate hybrid_block already uses, and the whole
parity forward runs inside it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d37db1077cb77ec08fb846485accd92ca39cd639)
---
 megatron/core/transformer/attention.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/megatron/core/transformer/attention.py b/megatron/core/transformer/attention.py
index 089cbf3ff..7b55090ca 100644
--- a/megatron/core/transformer/attention.py
+++ b/megatron/core/transformer/attention.py
@@ -1961,7 +1961,7 @@ class SelfAttention(Attention):
         If `output_gate` is True, then also derives `gate` tensor.
         If `split_qkv=False`, then the unsplit mixed_qkv tensor is returned.
         """
-        if self.config.inference_vllm_parity and not self.training:
+        if self.config.inference_vllm_parity and InferenceMode.is_active():
             from megatron.core.inference.vllm_parity import attention_qkv
 
             if output_gate or not split_qkv:
